NNAAMMEE
     rrppccbbiinndd — universal addresses to RPC program number mapper

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     rrppccbbiinndd [--66aaddiiLLllsswwWW] [--hh _b_i_n_d_i_p]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rrppccbbiinndd utility is a server that converts RPC program numbers into
     universal addresses.  It must be running on the host to be able to make
     RPC calls on a server on that machine.

     When an RPC service is started, it tells rrppccbbiinndd the address at which it
     is listening, and the RPC program numbers it is prepared to serve.  When
     a client wishes to make an RPC call to a given program number, it first
     contacts rrppccbbiinndd on the server machine to determine the address where RPC
     requests should be sent.

     The rrppccbbiinndd utility should be started before any other RPC service.  Nor‐
     mally, standard RPC servers are started by port monitors, so rrppccbbiinndd must
     be started before port monitors are invoked.

     When rrppccbbiinndd is started, it checks that certain name-to-address transla‐
     tion-calls function correctly.  If they fail, the network configuration
     databases may be corrupt.  Since RPC services cannot function correctly
     in this situation, rrppccbbiinndd reports the condition and terminates.

     The rrppccbbiinndd utility can only be started by the super-user.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
     --66      Bind to AF_INET6 (IPv6) addresses only.

     --aa      When debugging (--dd), do an abort on errors.

     --dd      Run in debug mode.  In this mode, rrppccbbiinndd will not fork when it
             starts, will print additional information during operation, and
             will abort on certain errors if --aa is also specified.  With this
             option, the name-to-address translation consistency checks are
             shown in detail.

     --hh _b_i_n_d_i_p
             IP addresses to bind to when servicing TCP and UDP requests.
             This option may be specified multiple times and is typically nec‐
             essary when running on a multi-homed host.  If no --hh option is
             specified, rrppccbbiinndd will bind to INADDR_ANY, which could lead to
             problems on a multi-homed host due to rrppccbbiinndd returning a UDP
             packet from a different IP address than it was sent to.  Note
             that when specifying IP addresses with --hh, rrppccbbiinndd will automati‐
             cally add 127.0.0.1 and if IPv6 is enabled, ::1 to the list.

     --ii      “Insecure” mode.  Allow calls to SET and UNSET from any host.
             Normally rrppccbbiinndd accepts these requests only from the loopback
             interface for security reasons.  This change is necessary for
             programs that were compiled with earlier versions of the rpc li‐
             brary and do not make those requests using the loopback inter‐
             face.

     --LL      Allow old-style local connections over the loopback interface.
             Without this flag, local connections are only allowed over a lo‐
             cal socket, _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_r_p_c_b_i_n_d_._s_o_c_k.

     --ll      Turn on libwrap connection logging.

     --ss      Cause rrppccbbiinndd to change to the user daemon as soon as possible.
             This causes rrppccbbiinndd to use non-privileged ports for outgoing con‐
             nections, preventing non-privileged clients from using rrppccbbiinndd to
             connect to services from a privileged port.

     --WW      Enable libwrap (TCP wrappers) support.

     --ww      Enable the warmstart feature.

             The warmstart feature saves RPC registrations on termination.
             Any saved RPC registrations are restored on restart if --ww is
             specified.  This feature helps avoid RPC service interruption
             when restarting rrppccbbiinndd.  warmstart support must be compiled in
             to rrppccbbiinndd.  Portmap registrations are stored in
             _/_t_m_p_/_p_o_r_t_m_a_p_._f_i_l_e.  rrppccbbiinndd registrations are stored in
             _/_t_m_p_/_r_p_c_b_i_n_d_._f_i_l_e.

NNOOTTEESS
     All RPC servers must be restarted if rrppccbbiinndd is restarted.

